1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,050
Can you show me Ingress?

2
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,429
An Ingress is a set of HTTP routing rules:

3
00:00:10,429 --> 00:00:17,637
"requests for app.local go to the frontend Service, requests for shop.local/api go to the backend Service".

4
00:00:17,637 --> 00:00:26,596
An ingress controller is the program (a reverse proxy running in the cluster) that reads those rules and actually routes the traffic.

5
00:00:26,596 --> 00:00:27,404
The analogy:

6
00:00:27,404 --> 00:00:34,275
Services are the departments of a company; the Ingress is the reception desk with one public entrance,

7
00:00:34,275 --> 00:00:40,675
reading the visitor's request ("I am here for accounting") and sending them to the right floor.

8
00:00:41,233 --> 00:00:49,178
Exposing every application with its own NodePort or LoadBalancer Service (lesson 10) does not scale:

9
00:00:49,178 --> 00:00:54,660
one random high port or one paid cloud load balancer per application,

10
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,712
no host names, no shared TLS certificate, no paths.

11
00:00:58,712 --> 00:01:04,909
Web traffic wants one entrance (ports 80/443) and rules by host name and path.

12
00:01:04,909 --> 00:01:06,498
That is the Ingress.

13
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:10,653
And how does it actually work?

14
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,334
The Ingress object alone does nothing:

15
00:01:14,334 --> 00:01:17,469
without a controller, nobody reads it.

16
00:01:17,469 --> 00:01:24,892
A cluster can run several controllers; ingressClassName says which one handles an Ingress.

17
00:01:24,892 --> 00:01:29,924
Minikube's addon installs ingress-nginx with the class nginx.

18
00:01:29,924 --> 00:01:37,430
(The ingress-nginx project was retired upstream in 2026; other controllers such as Traefik,

19
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:41,224
and the newer Gateway API, use the same ideas:

20
00:01:41,224 --> 00:01:49,308
host and path rules to Services.) The controller itself is reached from outside through a Service:

21
00:01:49,308 --> 00:01:52,195
on Minikube a NodePort on the node.

22
00:01:53,933 --> 00:01:54,091
1.

